1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000


2
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,680
Good. At least you understand
that I have power.

3
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:11,880
You're fired.

4
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,280
PREVIOUSLY

5
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,760
Then what do you want me to do?

6
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,840
Go back to the construction site.

7
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:18,160
You have to stay here.

8
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,040
Everything your mom owns belongs to me.

9
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,520
Even her life

10
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,520
and every breath she takes.

11
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:28,720
Chayanee ordered Hathaya
to work overtime. Go help her.

12
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,240
Hey.

13
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:38,960
You worked all day and all night.
You should rest today.

14
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,800
I can't.

15
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:44,240
Chayanee won't allow it. She'll just find
an excuse to give us a hard time.

16
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:47,720
Don't force yourself if you can't take it.
I'm worried about you.

17
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:56,120
Well, now that you're done here,
where are you going?

18
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:59,280
I need to find a job.

19
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:03,560
I have to save money so I can
take my mom away and live with her.

20
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:08,960
Your father is doing well for himself now.

21
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,080
You could ask him for help.

22
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,079
I don't want to depend on him.
And don't bring him up again. Understand?

23
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:24,720
Besides, I have a good resume.
I'll find something.

24
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,400
Good luck. I know you can do it.

25
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,960
You too. Hang in there.

26
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:36,920
What?

27
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,280
-Your hand.
-What for?

28
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,280
Hang in there.

29
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,160
You too.

30
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,320
FOREMAN WANTED

31
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:32,800
Hello.

32
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,480
Hello, Uncle.

33
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,120
Where's Ramil?

34
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:41,040
I want to see him.

35
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:46,760
Someone told me he quit.
How is that possible?

36
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:50,240
Mr. Pichai cares about Ramil.
There's no way he would fire him.

37
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,440
What happened?

38
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,400
Well…

39
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:10,400
All I had to do was tell people
to blacklist you. No one will hire you.

40
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:16,200
But if I send a message
asking them to give you a job,

41
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,400
they'll change their minds.

42
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:25,240
I don't need anyone's help.

43
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,280
Come on.

44
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:34,160
Weren't you planning to take
your mom away and start a new life?

45
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,680
You need money.

46
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,800
Stop worrying so much about your pride.

47
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:44,400
What do you want?

48
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,160
Get down and beg me.

49
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:57,880
What dignity do you even have? Your father
abandoned you when you were growing up.

50
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:00,880
My father took pity

51
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:04,360
on you and your mother
and let you live under our roof.

52
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:08,720
You were like a couple of stray dogs.

53
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:12,680
You have no dignity, Ramil.

54
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:16,520
You're worthless. You're a parasite.

55
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:21,560
Go on. Get down on your knees.

56
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,520
Ramil, don't.

57
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:41,600
You don't have to kneel to anyone.
I'll help you.

58
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,120
Back off. It's none of your business.

59
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,000
Bow down.

60
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:22,640
Bow to me.

61
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:37,400
I knelt and paid my respects to you

62
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,640
as a way of thanking you

63
00:08:40,799 --> 00:08:42,760
for the help you gave me
when we were children.

64
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:45,080
But from now on,

65
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:48,080
we owe each other nothing.

66
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:53,040
And to be perfectly clear,

67
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,800
someone like you…

68
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,960
isn't worth bowing to.

69
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:04,680
But if you want me
to bow to you that badly,

70
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:06,880
wait a little longer.

71
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,000
I'll do it…

72
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,840
at your funeral.

73
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,120
Ramil.

74
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,920
So you're declaring yourself my enemy?

75
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:25,960
Just wait. I'll destroy your life.

76
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,440
Ramil. I need to talk to you.

77
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:54,240
We already talked. Stay away from me.

78
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:59,600
I know you were fired
and you're looking for work.

79
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,360
I'm doing well for myself now.

80
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:06,200
You don't need to work for anyone else.
I'll invest in you.

81
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,560
Start your own development.

82
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:12,760
Why won't you accept
that I'm trying to help?

83
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,720
I told you already. I don't have a father.

84
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:21,920
And from childhood until now,

85
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,520
I've survived on my own.

86
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:26,800
I don't need to depend on you.
I can live without you.

87
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:30,680
I know I was wrong. I won't make excuses.

88
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,960
If you never forgive me,
I can accept that.

89
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:39,200
Then what do you want?

90
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:44,240
Don't cut me out of your life.
Let me be your father.

91
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,080
Where are you going?

92
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,760
I'm moving out.

93
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:15,960
Put that away.

94
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:19,520
I'm going to find somewhere to rent.
I don't want to be a burden anymore.

95
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:23,480
I told you to put it away.

96
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,080
I've said what I needed to.

97
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,440
Enough.

98
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:32,040
Let me see.

99
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:35,320
You don't need any of it.

100
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:38,360
Take everything out.

101
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,960
Pick everything up and go back upstairs.

102
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:45,000
They're only clothes. I can buy new ones.

103
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:52,880
Why do you want to keep me here?
You've never valued me.

104
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:57,280
I want to be treated like a person.
I don't want to be your obedient pet.

105
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,520
I asked you before whether
you ever loved me.

106
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,920
You couldn't answer
because you never loved me.

107
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:05,360
You only wanted to use me.

108
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:09,000
You brought me here because you
needed someone to raise your son

109
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:11,000
and take care of everything in the house.

110
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:13,280
You wanted a housekeeper, not a wife.

111
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:17,320
And you already promised me.

112
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,560
You said if I gave you my assets,

113
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:22,000
you would let me go. Please.

114
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:25,280
Sanguansri. Come back. Come back!

115
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,920
I said come back.

116
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,080
Sanguansri.

117
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,480
You don't have the right
to do whatever you want.

118
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:33,720
I'm the only one who decides
whether you stay or go.

119
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:36,080
Get back inside.

120
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:38,600
I'm not staying.
I don't want to be your pet anymore.

121
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:41,720
Oh, really? I told you to go back--

122
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:42,680
-No!
-Stop, Saksit!

123
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,560
Hey.

124
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:51,000
What the hell does this have to do
with you? You drove onto my property.

125
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:53,200
You're trespassing. Get out.

126
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:55,920
I'm not leaving until this is settled.

127
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:58,120
Fine. Raiwin.

128
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:01,640
Call the police and have them
drag him out of here.

129
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,840
I came here to talk.

130
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:09,920
You and Sanguansri aren't happy together.
Why keep forcing this?

131
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,960
I came to take her away with me.

132
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:16,200
You're despicable.
You abandoned your wife and son.

133
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:19,160
I took them in
and supported them for years.

134
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,600
You know how much money I spent?

135
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:23,240
Now you have the nerve
to ask for your wife back?

136
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,480
How much do you want?

137
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:27,120
Now that's how I like it.

138
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:31,000
This is how a rich man should talk.

139
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:34,920
How much do you want
to divorce Sanguansri?

140
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:40,120
Twenty million.

141
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:43,400
You already took her money
and her property. That still isn't enough?

142
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:50,360
I'll give you ten million. Refuse,
and I'll have a lawyer file for divorce.

143
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,200
This case won't be difficult to win.

144
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:56,640
You've been abusing her all along.

145
00:13:57,760 --> 00:14:01,360
Your choice. Ten million,
or not a single baht.

146
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,440
Tomorrow.

147
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,560
Bring me the money.

148
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,960
Then you can take your wife back.

149
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,040
I need to speak to her privately.

150
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,160
Privately?

151
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:28,200
Fine. Talk privately.

152
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:43,920
Are you hurt?

153
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,320
No. I'm fine.

154
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,280
But you shouldn't get into trouble for me.

155
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,680
Don't think like that.

156
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,920
I need to make up
for abandoning you and our son.

157
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,440
But where are you going to get the money?

158
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:06,640
I told you. The business I started
with my friend is doing well.

159
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,880
I have enough now to help you

160
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:12,240
start a new life.

161
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:20,240
You don't have to forgive me.
You don't even have to love me again.

162
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:24,320
I just want you and our son
to live comfortably.

163
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:27,000
I'll come back for you tomorrow.

164
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,800
I'll be waiting.

165
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,920
You're the one

166
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,200
who told him about me, weren't you?

167
00:15:56,040 --> 00:16:00,840
Mr. Anon is very worried about you.
And he's proven that he can change.

168
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:05,400
He has a stable career now.
I want you to forgive your father.

169
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:09,480
No.

170
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:11,920
I've been hurt

171
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:14,200
too badly to forgive him.

172
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:16,600
And I'm scared…

173
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,640
that I'll get hurt all over again.

174
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:23,960
It's better if he stays out of our lives.

175
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,400
And one more thing.

176
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,080
Don't help him either.

177
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,280
Hathaya.

178
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:49,800
Promise me.

179
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:53,120
Okay.

180
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,440
It's Ramil's dad.

181
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,599
Can we talk tomorrow?

182
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,840
Hello, Uncle.

183
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:34,560
Were you just at the development?

184
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:39,360
I had something to take care of.
Ramil won't answer my calls. Where is he?

185
00:17:40,240 --> 00:17:44,040
Actually, Ramil already got upset with me

186
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:45,840
for telling you what happened.

187
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:51,440
I'm sorry I got you into trouble too.

188
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:56,000
But this is important.
I need to see Ramil.

189
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:04,920
I'm going to give Saksit money
to buy Sanguansri's freedom.

190
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:09,320
I want Ramil with me
to bring his mom home.

191
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:13,120
She'll be so happy if he comes with me.

192
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,040
Can you help me one more time?

193
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:38,000
Hello, Ramil.

194
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:42,040
I'm going out at noon to buy
some things for the workers.

195
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,720
Can you come meet me?

196
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:48,320
Okay. Yes.

197
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:54,800
I arranged for Ramil to meet you.

198
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:00,800
Thank you so much. Truly.

199
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:04,200
Today is going to be
the happiest day of my life.

200
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:06,680
We'll finally be together as a family.

201
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,720
Yes.

202
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,680
Thank you.

203
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:24,200
I'm here. Where are you?

204
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:25,720
Ramil.

205
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,560
What do you need?
I'll help you pick it out.

206
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,000
You.

207
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:59,560
Your father has something important
he needs to talk to you about.

208
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,960
Why did you do this?

209
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:06,440
I trusted you, but you lied to me.

210
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:09,880
I'm sorry I broke my promise.

211
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:13,040
Please listen to me first.
Your father has something--

212
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,800
I told you already.

213
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,880
I don't have a father. My father is dead.

214
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:23,000
Ramil, wait.

215
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:28,680
Uncle.

216
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:31,760
Please wait here. I'll go talk to Ramil.

217
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:32,720
Hey.

218
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:38,080
Enough. You've already
done so much to help me.

219
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:41,080
I don't want Ramil getting
even angrier with you.

220
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:45,040
I want Ramil to go with you.

221
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:49,920
It's almost time for my appointment.
I need to settle things with Saksit.

222
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:56,320
If I can get his mom out of there,
maybe Ramil will forgive me.

223
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:59,600
I'm rooting for you.

224
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,200
Thank you so much.

225
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:04,040
Take care, Uncle.

226
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Wow.

227
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:20,000
What are you standing there for?

228
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:22,880
Take her suitcase outside.

229
00:21:23,480 --> 00:21:27,120
Sanguansri's husband
is coming to pick her up.

230
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:31,080
She can't wait to get out of this house.

231
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:33,760
Your boss

232
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:36,360
is dying to get out of here.

233
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:42,000
You look beautiful today.

234
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:46,880
You must be desperate
to see your old husband again.

235
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,640
I just want to live with my son.

236
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:51,640
I want us to have a life together.

237
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:55,920
What time are you meeting Anon?

238
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,960
It's almost time.

239
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:05,480
Raiwin, come out with me.

240
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,400
Where are you going?

241
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:11,840
I arranged to collect
the money somewhere else.

242
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,880
Once I have it,

243
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,480
I'll let him come pick you up.

244
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:20,320
Why not meet him here?
Then once it's settled, I can leave.

245
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:24,360
You hate looking at me that much?

246
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:28,360
You can't wait to get away from me?

247
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:31,200
Let me tell you something.
I arranged for my lawyer

248
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:33,480
to prepare written documents.

249
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:36,840
My lawyer is sick.
I don't want to waste time,

250
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:39,080
so I'm meeting him at his house.

251
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:42,320
And I told your ex-husband
to meet us there too.

252
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,560
Look.

253
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:54,280
I had your favorite food prepared.
Have it before you go.

254
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:57,640
Enjoy.

255
00:22:57,720 --> 00:23:00,520
Eat plenty. Drink lots of water too.

256
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:02,600
In case you shed some tears.

257
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:05,960
Oh.

258
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:10,200
I'm just happy for you.
I imagine you'll be crying with joy

259
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:15,320
once you finally get out of this house.

260
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:35,200
Hello.

261
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,680
I'm heading out now.

262
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:40,680
Make sure your money is ready.

263
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:42,560
I have the full amount.

264
00:23:43,480 --> 00:23:45,240
Once the papers are signed, I'll get her.

265
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:49,480
Come on, Raiwin.

266
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:05,240
Ramil, wait. Wait.

267
00:24:07,960 --> 00:24:09,920
I know you're upset.

268
00:24:10,960 --> 00:24:13,080
I broke your trust.

269
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:17,760
But I just don't want you
to regret things the way I do.

270
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,560
I don't have a father.

271
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:28,240
The grandmother I loved is gone.

272
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,800
My mother only keeps creating problems.

273
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:35,240
I have no one left.

274
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:39,400
But you still have them.

275
00:24:42,040 --> 00:24:46,040
Your father is trying
to change himself for his family.

276
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,800
He wants you to be proud of him just once.

277
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,600
I know I was wrong.

278
00:24:58,760 --> 00:25:02,680
I only wanted all of you
to be together again.

279
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:12,120
Father, mother, and son.

280
00:25:14,760 --> 00:25:16,360
I lied…

281
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:20,000
because I wanted to see you happy.

282
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:24,120
But I'm happier without him.

283
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,880
But you're talking about your father.

284
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:30,640
He worked to get the money

285
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:32,880
to buy your mother's freedom.

286
00:25:36,040 --> 00:25:37,760
He wanted you to go with him.

287
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:42,600
He wanted you to be the one
to bring your mother out of that house.

288
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:47,640
So she could be proud of you.

289
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:56,760
I know he's disappointed and hurt you
more times than you can count.

290
00:25:58,680 --> 00:26:01,000
But can you give your father
one more chance…

291
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:05,800
before it's too late?

292
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,440
I'm going to get my mom.

293
00:26:57,240 --> 00:27:00,400
Dad, your lawyer's house isn't this way.

294
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:04,680
Who told you I was going
to my lawyer's house?

295
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:07,680
Then where are you meeting Ramil's dad?

296
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:16,960
Dad, what are you doing?

297
00:27:35,480 --> 00:27:36,480
Mom.

298
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:41,760
-Where are they?
-They went out.

299
00:27:42,880 --> 00:27:45,480
Wasn't Uncle Anon supposed
to bring the money here?

300
00:27:46,080 --> 00:27:48,640
Mr. Saksit said they'd settle
everything at the lawyer's.

301
00:27:48,720 --> 00:27:51,480
He said once it was finished,
Anon would come here to get me.

302
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:54,640
Then why did they need
to meet somewhere else?

303
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:58,080
Ramil, I have a bad feeling.
I want to go find your father.

304
00:27:59,080 --> 00:28:02,720
I'll call Uncle Anon and ask where he is.

305
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:09,080
Hello, dear.

306
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:10,280
Hello, Uncle.

307
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:15,240
Where are you meeting Mr. Saksit?
Could you share your location with me?

308
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:17,200
Is something wrong?

309
00:28:18,080 --> 00:28:19,200
So…

310
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:22,280
Ramil is going with you.

311
00:28:23,080 --> 00:28:25,680
And he wants to bring Aunt Sanguansri too.

312
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:28,320
Once everything is settled,
all of you can leave together.

313
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:34,480
We're finally going to be
together as a family?

314
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:37,200
Thank you so much.

315
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:52,120
He sent the location.

316
00:29:07,040 --> 00:29:09,800
I want a big house. Several bedrooms.

317
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:13,280
That way, when my son has a family,
there'll be room for my grandchildren.

318
00:29:17,280 --> 00:29:18,360
Soon,

319
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:21,560
we'll all be together.

320
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:24,160
Father, mother, and son.

321
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:53,840
Why did you stop?

322
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:55,600
Go. Follow him.

323
00:29:57,480 --> 00:29:59,680
Dad, do you even realize
what you're doing?

324
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:03,040
Of course. I'm not going to be humiliated.
If he takes my woman,

325
00:30:03,120 --> 00:30:06,560
I'll kill him, take his cash,
and keep his woman working for me.

326
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:10,320
You're trying to kill someone.
You could get the death penalty.

327
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:12,680
I know. Stop talking. Follow him.

328
00:30:12,760 --> 00:30:14,400
Hurry.

329
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:16,000
No. Enough.

330
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:18,520
How can I stop now? He saw my face.

331
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:20,280
He knows I shot him.

332
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:23,160
If he survives, he'll come after us.

333
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:26,320
You and I will both
become suspects and go to prison.

334
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:29,280
And you'll be charged as my accomplice.

335
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:31,560
Go. Hurry.

336
00:30:56,760 --> 00:30:57,720
Dad.

337
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:02,520
He's dead. Let's go. Someone could see us.

338
00:31:02,600 --> 00:31:04,000
-Come on.
-Wait.

339
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:07,880
Dad, what are you doing?

340
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:10,400
Dad.

341
00:31:18,280 --> 00:31:21,120
-He's still alive.
-You bastards.

342
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:27,840
Help. Help me.

343
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:36,080
Kill him.

344
00:31:36,680 --> 00:31:37,560
Shoot him.

345
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:39,720
No.

346
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:45,520
I can't do it, Dad.

347
00:31:46,320 --> 00:31:48,320
Please don't make me.

348
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:49,680
Make you?

349
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,120
Hey.

350
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:53,520
You want me to kill you too?

351
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:56,120
Dad.

352
00:31:57,560 --> 00:31:59,600
I'm your son.

353
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:02,800
You're my son. And I'd still kill you

354
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:05,280
if you betrayed me.

355
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:09,680
If you want the money, take it.

356
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:13,480
Just let me go. I…

357
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:16,760
I only want to live with my wife and son.

358
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:18,760
Your wife?

359
00:32:19,760 --> 00:32:21,720
Kill him. Now!

360
00:32:22,600 --> 00:32:25,160
Someone like you isn't worth bowing to.

361
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:28,120
But if you want me
to bow to you that badly,

362
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:30,520
I'll do it…

363
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:34,640
at your funeral.

364
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:53,880
Hey. What are you standing there for?

365
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:56,720
Move. Someone could come. Drive.

366
00:32:58,080 --> 00:32:59,320
Hurry. Get in.

367
00:33:03,040 --> 00:33:05,240
Hurry. Go.

368
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:23,880
That's Uncle Anon's car.

369
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:28,320
Anon.

370
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:38,920
Ramil.

371
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:43,040
-Dad.
-Uncle.

372
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:45,120
Anon.

373
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:47,000
What happened?

374
00:33:47,520 --> 00:33:49,360
I'm sorry.

375
00:33:52,840 --> 00:33:55,040
I couldn't buy your freedom.

376
00:33:56,760 --> 00:33:58,960
What happened?

377
00:34:02,480 --> 00:34:04,360
They took the money.

378
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:19,480
I'm so happy

379
00:34:20,719 --> 00:34:22,199
you came to see me, son.

380
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:34,920
I bought you a house.

381
00:34:36,159 --> 00:34:37,320
I finally bought it.

382
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:49,000
I sold our house before.

383
00:34:50,760 --> 00:34:52,400
I hurt you so badly.

384
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:57,440
Let me make it right, son.

385
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:03,240
I bought a big house…

386
00:35:05,560 --> 00:35:07,360
so you can live there with your mom.

387
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:16,800
I chose one with many bedrooms too.

388
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:20,880
When you have a family…

389
00:35:23,200 --> 00:35:25,520
there'll be room for the grandchildren.

390
00:35:38,760 --> 00:35:40,520
If you can forgive me…

391
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:51,240
please let me come visit you
and your mom sometimes.

392
00:35:53,640 --> 00:35:54,560
No.

393
00:35:58,320 --> 00:35:59,480
You don't have to visit.

394
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:06,440
You have to come live with us.

395
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:16,440
I forgive you.

396
00:36:19,080 --> 00:36:20,040
Please, Dad.

397
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:22,560
Come live with us, Dad.

398
00:36:24,160 --> 00:36:25,400
Please, Dad.

399
00:36:26,080 --> 00:36:28,160
-Dad! No.
-Anon!

400
00:36:28,880 --> 00:36:31,760
Anon! Anon!

401
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:33,280
Dad.

402
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:35,800
Come live with us.

403
00:36:42,080 --> 00:36:43,920
‎Come live with us.

404
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:49,520
It was exactly like you said.

405
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:55,240
By the time I forgave my father…

406
00:38:01,840 --> 00:38:03,280
it was too late.

407
00:38:10,720 --> 00:38:13,040
It's never too late for love.

408
00:38:16,200 --> 00:38:19,960
You may feel like you lost him.

409
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:23,720
Well, you did.

410
00:38:26,720 --> 00:38:28,880
But what matters most is that

411
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:30,760
you forgave him…

412
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:34,720
accepted him…

413
00:38:36,520 --> 00:38:38,720
and truly loved him.

414
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:47,560
I believe that wherever
your father's spirit has gone…

415
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:51,320
he's at peace…

416
00:38:53,560 --> 00:38:55,880
because he knew how much you loved him.

417
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:04,920
When I lost Grandma…

418
00:39:10,320 --> 00:39:12,440
you told me to keep living…

419
00:39:15,240 --> 00:39:16,760
for the people I love.

420
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:24,880
I want to tell you the same thing now.

421
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:32,040
Keep going…

422
00:39:34,520 --> 00:39:36,040
for your mother.

423
00:40:14,240 --> 00:40:15,840
Dad, have you heard about Ramil?

424
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:17,840
What?

425
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:21,400
Is he going to kill himself and follow
his father? Throw himself into a fire

426
00:40:21,480 --> 00:40:23,200
and become one of the Pleiades?

427
00:40:25,320 --> 00:40:26,680
No, Dad.

428
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:31,920
Ramil inherited everything
from his father.

429
00:40:32,560 --> 00:40:34,560
-Hello, Mr. Ramil.
-Hello.

430
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:36,480
I'm Mr. Anon's lawyer.

431
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:40,400
He left a will in this document.

432
00:40:44,640 --> 00:40:47,520
I'll handle the transfer

433
00:40:47,600 --> 00:40:49,280
of all his assets to you.

434
00:40:51,040 --> 00:40:52,000
Thank you.

435
00:41:03,320 --> 00:41:05,720
His father brought me ten million.

436
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:08,760
What could he possibly have left? Debt?

437
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:13,040
I checked. There's more.

438
00:41:20,960 --> 00:41:24,800
Dad bought a house
in the development in my name.

439
00:41:26,720 --> 00:41:30,640
He also left me all his shares.
They're worth over a hundred million.

440
00:41:31,160 --> 00:41:34,920
Plus land and other assets.

441
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:40,240
His father left him everything.

442
00:41:41,520 --> 00:41:44,360
He practically never has to work
another day in his life.

443
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:47,920
That parasite.

444
00:41:49,160 --> 00:41:51,200
You think you're going
to rise above me now?

445
00:41:57,120 --> 00:41:59,920
Now that you have everything,

446
00:42:00,440 --> 00:42:02,200
what are you going to do?

447
00:42:04,920 --> 00:42:06,840
While the house is being built…

448
00:42:09,080 --> 00:42:11,200
I'll find somewhere temporary
for Mom to live.

449
00:42:12,560 --> 00:42:15,880
Your mom is at Saksit's house right now

450
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:20,760
packing her things. We should hurry over
and tell her the good news.

451
00:42:23,240 --> 00:42:24,080
Let's go.

452
00:42:30,560 --> 00:42:31,880
Why did you come back?

453
00:42:31,960 --> 00:42:35,400
You already left this house.

454
00:42:35,960 --> 00:42:38,240
So leave. Get out.

455
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:40,520
I changed my mind. I'm not leaving.

456
00:42:42,720 --> 00:42:46,240
Your husband dies
and now you've lost your mind?

457
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:51,160
Anon was supposed to take me away.
He's dead now. Where am I supposed to go?

458
00:42:51,240 --> 00:42:54,680
Why don't you go live with your son?

459
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:56,360
His life is pretty comfortable now.

460
00:43:00,280 --> 00:43:01,200
Mom.

461
00:43:02,200 --> 00:43:03,080
Come with me.

462
00:43:03,880 --> 00:43:05,040
I'll take care of you.

463
00:43:06,640 --> 00:43:10,600
You're unemployed and already struggling.
I don't want to become a burden.

464
00:43:11,840 --> 00:43:14,720
Uncle Anon left everything to Ramil.

465
00:43:17,040 --> 00:43:20,200
That's right, Mom. Dad bought me a house.

466
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:22,240
He left me his shares in the company.

467
00:43:22,320 --> 00:43:24,480
The assets are worth
more than a hundred million.

468
00:43:29,720 --> 00:43:33,280
From now on, we don't
have to struggle anymore.

469
00:43:34,120 --> 00:43:36,320
We don't have to be anyone's
parasites ever again.

470
00:43:37,640 --> 00:43:40,360
While we wait
for the new house to be finished,

471
00:43:40,440 --> 00:43:42,560
I'll find you a nice place to stay.

472
00:43:43,360 --> 00:43:44,200
Come with me.

473
00:43:47,040 --> 00:43:48,640
I want to stay here.

474
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:53,920
Why, Mom?

475
00:43:55,360 --> 00:43:56,320
Oh.

476
00:43:58,760 --> 00:44:00,280
Did they threaten you again?

477
00:44:00,360 --> 00:44:04,520
Hey. Don't blame me.

478
00:44:05,720 --> 00:44:07,600
Go, sweetheart. I want to stay here.

479
00:44:07,680 --> 00:44:09,120
I don't understand.

480
00:44:09,640 --> 00:44:11,080
What happened?

481
00:44:11,160 --> 00:44:14,160
I have money now. I can take care of you.

482
00:44:14,240 --> 00:44:15,400
Come with me, Mom.

483
00:44:18,000 --> 00:44:19,640
I've been thinking about it.

484
00:44:20,440 --> 00:44:23,960
Mr. Saksit looked after me.
He gave me food and a place to live.

485
00:44:24,560 --> 00:44:26,880
Now that we have money,
walking away from him

486
00:44:26,960 --> 00:44:28,520
would feel too selfish.

487
00:44:28,600 --> 00:44:31,520
Mom, stop thinking like that.

488
00:44:31,600 --> 00:44:35,440
You've already repaid them
far more than they ever did for us.

489
00:44:35,520 --> 00:44:39,720
No one in this house truly means well.
They don't genuinely love anyone.

490
00:44:39,800 --> 00:44:41,680
All they care about is what they can get.

491
00:44:41,760 --> 00:44:43,480
Ramil, shut up.

492
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:47,320
You barge into my house
and insult us? Get out.

493
00:44:47,400 --> 00:44:49,720
I'll leave when my mom leaves.

494
00:44:49,800 --> 00:44:51,160
Then go with him.

495
00:44:53,240 --> 00:44:54,840
Maybe he'll finally stop barking.

496
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:57,760
I'm staying here.

497
00:44:57,840 --> 00:44:59,000
Dad.

498
00:45:00,120 --> 00:45:01,720
Throw them out.

499
00:45:02,320 --> 00:45:04,760
You don't like pets
that won't obey, do you?

500
00:45:07,440 --> 00:45:08,800
That's right, son.

501
00:45:09,880 --> 00:45:12,480
I enjoy training stubborn animals.

502
00:45:17,360 --> 00:45:19,400
I like breaking them until they obey.

503
00:45:26,840 --> 00:45:30,760
I'll allow you to stay in this house.

504
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:35,080
Mom. You're coming with me right now.

505
00:45:38,440 --> 00:45:40,400
Go. I'm staying here.

506
00:45:42,760 --> 00:45:44,000
I don't understand.

507
00:45:44,760 --> 00:45:47,440
Before, you wanted to leave with me.

508
00:45:47,960 --> 00:45:49,240
And now,

509
00:45:50,200 --> 00:45:52,040
you want to put the collar back on?

510
00:45:54,760 --> 00:45:56,560
You want to be their pet that badly?

511
00:46:04,240 --> 00:46:05,880
Get out. Now.

512
00:46:13,320 --> 00:46:14,240
Fine.

513
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:17,960
I'll go.

514
00:46:21,280 --> 00:46:22,960
This is the worst day of my life, Mom.

515
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:27,600
I already lost Dad.

516
00:46:31,160 --> 00:46:32,960
Do I have to lose you too?

517
00:47:02,920 --> 00:47:05,240
Ramil, let me out here.

518
00:47:07,320 --> 00:47:08,320
Where are you going?

519
00:47:08,960 --> 00:47:12,040
I need to take care of something.
I'll be back soon.

520
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:50,400
I don't have much time. What is it?

521
00:47:51,400 --> 00:47:55,120
What are you planning?
Why didn't you leave with Ramil?

522
00:47:57,600 --> 00:47:59,080
I already explained everything.

523
00:47:59,160 --> 00:48:01,280
If that's all you wanted to ask,
I have to go.

524
00:48:01,360 --> 00:48:02,600
Auntie.

525
00:48:03,560 --> 00:48:05,080
I don't believe you.

526
00:48:05,160 --> 00:48:08,360
Someone who loves her son
as much as you wouldn't do this.

527
00:48:09,720 --> 00:48:13,480
What are you planning? Please tell me.

528
00:48:13,560 --> 00:48:14,520
I want to help.

529
00:48:17,160 --> 00:48:19,720
I think they were involved
in Anon's death.

530
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:26,640
I've lived with them for a long time.
I know when something is wrong.

531
00:48:27,440 --> 00:48:30,880
Even the story about meeting
Anon at the lawyer's house.

532
00:48:32,960 --> 00:48:37,040
And now that I know how hard
Anon worked for me and our son,

533
00:48:38,120 --> 00:48:40,160
I have to get justice for him.

534
00:48:41,880 --> 00:48:45,080
I think you should tell Ramil.

535
00:48:45,160 --> 00:48:46,880
Then he won't misunderstand you.

536
00:48:48,040 --> 00:48:51,600
No. Ramil cannot know.
He has a hot temper.

537
00:48:52,520 --> 00:48:55,920
If he starts suspecting Saksit
was involved in Anon's death,

538
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:57,520
he won't stay quiet.

539
00:48:58,640 --> 00:49:00,920
That's exactly why
I have to stay close to Saksit.

540
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:03,120
I need to investigate everything myself.

541
00:49:04,800 --> 00:49:09,040
Promise me you won't tell anyone.
This has to stay between us.

542
00:49:10,840 --> 00:49:13,200
I'll help you however I can.

543
00:49:13,280 --> 00:49:16,480
If you need anything, tell me.

544
00:49:16,560 --> 00:49:19,400
Do not do this alone. It's too dangerous.

545
00:49:22,560 --> 00:49:23,800
I have to go.

546
00:49:25,120 --> 00:49:26,440
Take care of Ramil for me.

547
00:49:27,040 --> 00:49:27,920
I will.

548
00:49:39,760 --> 00:49:42,720
I'm glad your father is dead.

549
00:49:42,800 --> 00:49:45,240
NEXT EPISODE

550
00:49:45,320 --> 00:49:48,160
We need to finish the work
so Grandpa will be happy.

551
00:49:49,880 --> 00:49:53,360
You'll see that
this granddaughter you love

552
00:49:53,880 --> 00:49:57,160
is a hundred, a thousand times
better than that parasite.

553
00:49:57,240 --> 00:50:00,120
I'd like Nuchwara
and her son to stay here.

554
00:50:00,200 --> 00:50:02,280
Why do you care so much
and treat her so well

555
00:50:02,360 --> 00:50:04,160
when she's just Ramil's wife?

556
00:50:04,240 --> 00:50:06,160
And what if I'm more than that?

557
00:52:02,000 --> 00:52:04,000
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen

558
00:52:04,000 --> 00:52:05,000

